{"metadata":{"title":"color","symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL7MXLNoteV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/color"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/color"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLColor","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote","title":"MXLNote","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNote","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Notes are the most common type of MusicXML data. The MusicXML format distinguishes between elements used for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sound information and elements used for notation information (e.g., tie is used for sound, tied for notation)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus grace notes do not have a duration element. Cue notes have a duration element, as do forward elements,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"but no tie elements. Having these two types of information available can make interchange easier, as some","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"programs handle one type of information more readily than the other."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNote/color":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/color","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote\/color","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"title":"color","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"color","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","title":"MXLColor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"}}}